Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:35:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(trace): Optimize 0 keeps every traced point (ADR-395)

LightBurn documents Optimize 0 as "no merging", but here 0 meant a 0.85x
merge tolerance, so the low end of the slider still merged boundary
points into fewer vertices and curves (settings audit finding 17). Now:

- Optimize 0 switches merging off. Every mid-crack boundary point stays
  a vertex: no Douglas-Peucker merge, no spline resample, no cubic fit.
  The Smoothness-driven straight-run flattener still runs.
- Between 0 and the neutral 0.2 the tolerance rises from 0.25x (the
  floor the old code declared but never reached) to 1x. Below 0.25x the
  fitted curves' sampling emits more points than "no merging" does.
- 0.2 and above are unchanged.

Measured with the audit bench (12 exact-answer images) and the logo
and dragon fixtures:
- Line Art, Smooth and Edge Detection defaults: byte-identical.
- Corpus point totals at Optimize 0 / 0.01 / 0.1 / 0.2 / 2:
  Line Art 25787 / 18213 / 13811 / 11941 / 10362,
  Smooth 26213 / 14577 / 11196 / 9789 / 11059,
  Edge 29017 / 21531 / 15777 / 13650 / 10806.
- A 1-bit disc at 0 has exactly one vertex per boundary crack in every
  outline preset (385 points vs 129 at 0.2 in Line Art).

Sharp keeps its preset 0.15, which now means 0.8125x instead of
0.9625x. Corpus: IoU 0.9343 -> 0.9370, mean edge error 0.122 -> 0.116
px, p95 0.287 -> 0.263 px, nodes 15879 -> 17064. Logo 13063 -> 13442
points, dragon 306477 -> 326951. Sharp's half-width line tolerance
makes its 0.01-0.14 range emit more points than 0 on the corpus
(25225 at 0.01 vs 17705); the shapes stay within the tolerance.

